            "review_title": "Review at India Special Restaurant",
            "review_text": "hannostamm\nSiem Reap, Cambodia1028 contributions\n0\nAvoid, poor service and food.\nMar 2024 • Solo\nI had to stay near the airport for the night and craved Indian food. Couldn't be bothered to go downtown, where there are plenty of really good Indian restaurants. Mistake!!\n\nI arrived at 19:30 and all the staff were having dinner and I obviously disrupted them. \n\nOne staff reluctantly put me at a filthy table with a tablecloth that hadn't been washed in a long time, if ever. I waited to order but nobody showed up. I had to go out and find staff. When I asked why there was no service, it was made clear to me that the staff dinner takes precedence over paying customers.\n\nThe food did arrive eventually. I had asked for the Samosas as a starter, but everything came at once. The condiments for the Samosas were cheap chili sauce and ketchup. I have eaten in plenty of Indian restaurants, but this was a first.\n\nThe curry was absolutely tasteless. Hey had obviously taken pre-cooked chicken and threw it into a microwaved sauce. The oil had separated, so visually it was a disaster too.\n\nAvoid at all costs and spend the money on a Grab to go to a real restaurant.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nFind another restaurant.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten April 4, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
